message: >-
  Please cite the selected composition and its constituent contributions,
  this project and the upstream manuscript. The selected checkpoint is PR890
  with PR589; consult certificates/selected-result.json for publication status.
  Project-level authorship identifies the maintainer, not sole authorship of
  the community result. See CONTRIBUTORS.md and the frozen source notices.
title: "A sharper exponent for integer multiplication"
authors:
  - family-names: Colkitt
    given-names: Douglas
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
version: "community-frontier890-2026-10-13"
date-released: 2026-10-13
repository-code: "https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds"
url: "https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds"
abstract: >-
  Community research on integer multiplication. The selected maintainer-reviewed
  conditional finite composition has kappa = 1661957774647029/1000000000000000000
  = 0.001661957774647029. Chafik Boukhalfa's PR890 T21 whole-owner packing
  composes Jeremy Kothe's PR869/PR870 U8 delivery rewrite and Hao Yan's PR858
  T16 owner construction with DreamingOfClouds' PR589 bit supplier on eumemic's
  PR555, building on Chafik Boukhalfa's PR741 frames, Jeremy Kothe's X4/SW4
  chain, icekylinx's source gauge, Rohan Arun's recurrence correction and the
  cumulative community framework. Parallel constructions, verification tools
  and scoped research results are preserved. All-size/compiler,
  common-label/mutable-source, whole-call hosting, precision/tape,
  analytic-transfer and bit H1-H5 interfaces remain conditional.
  Finite checks do not constitute a complete Lean multiplication theorem.
